{
  "name": "swim_side",
  "//": "SWIMMING SIDEWAYS, authored travelling to the body's RIGHT; the left is the library's derived swim_side.mirror. A sidestroke on an upright body leaning 18 degrees into the travel: the leading (right) arm reaches out overhead to the side and pulls down to the hip, recovering folded across the chest; the trailing arm pushes the water away to the left; the legs scissor open and snap shut. Rotations: hips = lean Z (+ = right) of pitch X (+ = forward) of roll Y; every other part = sweep Y of flex X of abduction Z. A hanging limb: X negative = forward/up, positive = back; Z negative = the RIGHT limb out from the side. Knees +X bend, elbows -X bend. Hips pos in decimetres. All six swim clips share one 1600 ms period and one playhead (pose.cpp, the swim family), so a blend of two directions strokes in step.",
